LIMITATIONS

1. User limit. Use of the software is limited to a maximum number of Active
   Human Users, counted once per natural person across all deployments
   operated by you and your company. That maximum is the greater of:

   (a) ten (10); and

   (b) the number of Active Human Users permitted by the Commercial License
       Keys you hold that are valid and in force.

   Use above the applicable maximum is not licensed under these terms. The
   limit applies to every kind of use, including production, development,
   testing, staging, evaluation, demonstration, and internal training.

   Where the number of Active Human Users exceeds ten (10), every deployment
   operated by you and your company requires a valid Commercial License Key
   issued by the licensor for that deployment, whether or not any individual
   deployment on its own has more than ten (10) Active Human Users. A
   deployment does not violate this Limitation 1 for want of its own key during
   the first thirty (30) days after you create it or after you first exceed ten
   (10) Active Human Users, whichever is later. That period does not start
   again because you recreate, rebuild, replace, or move a deployment that
   serves substantially the same function or the same users.

   Where the software provides no key functionality for a deployment, you must
   request a Commercial License Key for it from the licensor within thirty (30)
   days of first exceeding ten (10) Active Human Users, stating the number of
   Active Human Users you need. Until the licensor issues a Commercial License
   Key for that deployment, the absence of that key does not violate this
   Limitation 1, and a number counts under (b) as though a key permitting it
   were in force: the number stated in your request until the licensor responds
   to it, and after that the number the licensor sets in its response. You must
   pay the fee for that number under the licensor's published pricing for the
   period concerned, and the number counts under (b) only while you do. This
   paragraph ceases to apply when the licensor issues a key for that
   deployment.

   The licensor may issue trial keys for evaluation on request, at its
   discretion. A trial key is a Commercial License Key for the trial term
   stated in it.

2. No splitting to stay within the limit. You may not operate more than one
   deployment, use components of the software separately, create or use
   additional legal entities, or divide users, accounts, or workloads, for
   the purpose or with the effect of understating the number of Active Human
   Users across the deployments operated by you and your company, or of
   presenting use that is outside the Free Community tier as use within it.
   Sharing a single user account among several natural persons does not reduce
   the number of Active Human Users.

   An arrangement adopted for genuine business reasons other than the Active
   Human User limit, and a count that proves too low despite having been
   made in good faith, are not by themselves violations of this Limitation 2.

3. Managed and hosted services. You may not, without a Partner License:

   (a) provide the software, or any of its features or functionality, to any
       third party as a hosted or managed service; or

   (b) offer the software, or any of its features or functionality, to any
       third party under your own brand or as your own product or service.

   Paragraph (a) applies whether the functionality is provided directly,
   through a modified version or a derivative work, or through any interface,
   front end, gateway, or application programming interface that makes it
   available; whether or not the software has been modified; and whether the
   software runs on infrastructure operated by you, by the third party, or by
   anyone else. It includes software-as-a-service, platform-as-a-service,
   multi-tenant hosting, and similar offerings.

   Providing professional services to a third party in respect of a deployment
   that the third party operationally controls — including installing,
   configuring, integrating, administering, monitoring, and supporting it —
   is not itself a hosted or managed service, provided that the third party
   holds its own Commercial License Key for that deployment or its use of it
   is within its own Free Community tier, that you do not provide access to
   that deployment to anyone other than that third party, its personnel, and
   the users it permits, and that paragraph (b) does not apply to what you
   offer.

   A third party has "operational control" of a deployment only if it decides
   whether and where the deployment runs, it owns or contracts in its own name
   for the infrastructure the deployment runs on, and it can at any time take
   over or end the deployment's administration. Administering or monitoring a
   deployment for a third party that operationally controls it is not, by
   itself, operating that deployment. The meaning of "control" in DEFINITIONS
   does not apply to this paragraph.

4. Commercial redistribution. You may not sell, resell, sublicense, rent,
   lease, or bundle the software or any derivative work, and you may not
   charge any third party for the software or for access to it, without a
   Partner License. You may provide an unmodified copy of the software to a
   third party free of charge, and you may charge for your own professional
   services (such as installation, configuration, integration, or support),
   provided that you pass these terms on to the recipient as required under
   NOTICES and that you do not provide a copy to a recipient that you know, or
   reasonably should know, will use the software outside its own Free
   Community tier and without a Commercial License Key covering that use.

5. Derivative works. You may modify the software and use derivative works for
   the internal purposes of you and your company, subject to Limitation 1. You
   may not distribute, make available, or deploy a derivative work for or to
   any third party without a Partner License. Submitting a contribution to the
   licensor under FEEDBACK AND CONTRIBUTIONS is not a violation of this
   Limitation 5.

6. License keys and limits. You may not move, change, disable, circumvent,
   prevent, block, or otherwise interfere with the operation of the license
   key functionality or of the Active Human User limit in the software, and
   you may not manipulate the data on which the Active Human User count is
   based, in each case for the purpose of using the software above the
   applicable maximum, without a required Commercial License Key, or beyond a
   key's term. You may not remove or obscure functionality in the software
   that a license key protects in order to use that functionality without a
   key.

   Restricting a deployment's network access, including operating it in an
   environment with no network access at all, is not a violation of this
