8. Determining and confirming your use. Where the number of Active Human Users
   across the deployments operated by you and your company is, or may
   reasonably be, more than ten (10) or more than half the applicable maximum,
   whichever is lower, or where the licensor has asked you to confirm that
   number, you must keep records sufficient to determine it, using the counts
   the software produces and, for any access the software cannot count, a
   reasonable good-faith estimate.

   If the licensor has a reasonable basis to believe that your use exceeds the
   applicable maximum, the licensor may request written confirmation of that
   number. You will provide it within thirty (30) days of the request. This
   Limitation 8 does not entitle the licensor to access your systems, your
   deployments, or your data.

